<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>ILLUSTRATIVE ussf-266 ascent</name><description>ILLUSTRATIVE ASCENT ECEF — Falcon 9 USSF-266 (SLC-4E) — NOT OFFICIAL TELEMETRY
PRE-FLIGHT. T0 is the window open 2026-11-24T15:55:00Z (Tue 24 Nov 7:55 a.m. PT), four-hour window to 19:55Z. Backup 2026-11-25T15:46:00Z.
SpaceX https://www.spacex.com/launches/ussf266 : MECO 2:26, stage sep 2:29, SES-1 2:36, fairing 2:56, entry 6:03-6:27, landing burn 8:01, landing 8:23 on OCISLY. 29th flight. SECO, orbit and deploy unpublished. Payload classified; no satellite count.
Loft: FALCON 9 FAMILY SURROGATE, the same Iridium NEXT-7 altitude and downrange rows as USSF-317 / USSF-627, laid on this flight&#x27;s azimuth. https://github.com/shahar603/Telemetry-Data/tree/master/Iridium%20NEXT%207
  Those sample times match this flight: MECO T+146 s, SES-1 T+156 s, fairing T+176 s. FILE ENDS AT T+508 s (telemetry end).
Azimuth 193.41 deg: bearing from SLC-4E to the centroid of NOTAM NTTT A1483/26 (USSF266-TH3 debris return; 28.779S 134.454W, 7199 km). https://space-notices.com/notice/notam-NTTT-A1483%2F26
  Non-rotating inclination 101.00 deg. The stage-1 box MMFO B4504/26 (centroid bearing about 169.4 deg) is not used; a 193.41 deg rhumb misses it by about 280 km. https://space-notices.com/notice/notam-MMFO-B4504%2F26
ASSUMPTION: plane after the loft and the parking orbit are not this flight&#x27;s. Inclination unpublished. ILLUSTRATIVE.
Velocity = d/dt of the family altitude and ground range, laid on this azimuth (Earth-relative ECEF).
Pad (LL2): 34.632000N -120.611000E. Frame: WGS-84 ECEF, positions km, velocities km/s.
Constant-azimuth rhumb Az=193.41 deg from pad (spherical R=6371.0088 km). Velocity ECEF: finite difference of ECEF position.
T0 used: 2026-11-24T15:55:00Z. Re-run with another T0 by shifting utc_iso only; ECEF geometry is Earth-fixed.</description>
